<section class="topic-kpi-section" aria-labelledby="kpi-topic-heading">
  <h2 id="kpi-topic-heading" class="kpi-topic-title">suggested KPIs for this topic</h2>

  <p class="kpi-topic-intro">
    These KPIs help your team build habits that uncover cross-selling opportunities consistently,
    not accidentally. They measure collaboration, awareness of other disciplines, proactive inquiry,
    and how effectively your firm presents integrated solutions instead of siloed services.
  </p>

  <div class="expandable-container kpi-expandable-container">


    <!-- 1. Pathway Building: Routine Cross-Discipline Contact -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-pathways">
        pathway building: routine cross-discipline contact
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-pathways">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Complete at least one cross-discipline activity (knowledge swap, coffee talk, prompt, etc.) per month.</li>
          <li>Keep a roster of “active pathways” — departments you connected with in the last 90 days.</li>
          <li>Ensure each business unit meets at least once per quarter with another unit.</li>
          <li>Document insights from each activity to track recurring opportunities.</li>
          <li>Reduce the number of departments that go more than 6 months without meaningful cross-contact.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- 2. Proactive Inquiry (Not Waiting for the Opportunity) -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-inquiry">
        proactive inquiry (not waiting for the opportunity)
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-inquiry">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Ask at least three cross-selling questions in every major client or project review meeting.</li>
          <li>Log potential cross-service fits even when no immediate opportunity exists.</li>
          <li>Identify at least two clients per month who could benefit from another service line.</li>
          <li>Proactively share early client intel with relevant business units.</li>
          <li>Reduce passive “wait and see” behaviour by using structured inquiry at every checkpoint.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- 3. Internal Awareness of Other Disciplines -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-awareness">
        internal awareness of other disciplines
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-awareness">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Attend at least one session per year where another unit explains its services and BD approach.</li>
          <li>Update cross-service cheat sheets annually (what each team sells, to whom, common triggers).</li>
          <li>Ensure every team member can name at least three services outside their discipline relevant to their clients.</li>
          <li>Maintain a directory of discipline-specific “cross-selling cues” (signs a client may need that service).</li>
          <li>Improve the percentage of staff who feel confident explaining at least one other discipline’s value.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- 4. Opportunity Flow & Sharing Behaviour -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-opportunities">
        opportunity flow &amp; sharing behaviour
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-opportunities">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Track how many opportunities are shared across business units each quarter.</li>
          <li>Reduce the number of opportunities discovered “too late” to influence.</li>
          <li>Ensure each significant client account has a cross-discipline growth plan.</li>
          <li>Monitor how many opportunities lead to follow-up meetings or intel exchanges.</li>
          <li>Identify bottlenecks (where information tends to stop moving) and address them.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- 5. Client Experience & Integrated Solutions -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-integrated">
        client experience &amp; integrated solutions
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-integrated">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Present integrated solutions (not siloed services) in at least 60–80% of major proposals.</li>
          <li>Review key clients annually to identify missing services they may value.</li>
          <li>Increase the number of multi-discipline projects with this client year over year.</li>
          <li>Document how cross-discipline collaboration improved outcomes on completed work.</li>
          <li>Use stories of successful cross-discipline wins in BD and proposal messaging.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- 6. Cultural Shifts & Overcoming Barriers -->
    <div class="expandable-item">
      <h3 class="expandable-title" data-target="kpi-culture">
        cultural shifts &amp; overcoming barriers
        <svg class="expand-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          viewBox="0 0 331.65 100.99" style="width:24px">
          <polygon fill="#4e50a2"
            points="0 0 161.57 100.99 331.65 0 0 0"/>
        </svg>
      </h3>

      <div class="expandable-content" id="kpi-culture">
        <ul class="kpi-list">
          <li>Reduce reported discomfort about “bothering other departments” over time.</li>
          <li>Track how many staff voluntarily initiate cross-discipline contact (not just respond).</li>
          <li>Celebrate cross-selling wins internally to reinforce healthy behaviour.</li>
          <li>Use the Twennie prompt set monthly until the pathways become habit.</li>
          <li>Decrease reliance on monthly BD meetings as the only source of cross-discipline discussion.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>


  </div>

  <p class="kpi-topic-footer">
    Choose a KPI from each category to build a culture where cross-selling is natural,
    frequent, and built into normal operations — not a once-a-month topic that fades away
    until next time.
  </p>
</section>


<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    const titles = document.querySelectorAll('.kpi-expandable-container .expandable-title');

    titles.forEach(function (title) {
      title.addEventListener('click', function () {
        const parent = this.closest('.expandable-item');
        const targetId = this.getAttribute('data-target');
        const content = document.getElementById(targetId);
        if (!parent || !content) return;

        const isActive = parent.classList.contains('active');
        parent.classList.toggle('active', !isActive);
        content.style.display = !isActive ? 'block' : 'none';
      });
    });
  });
</script>
